course: dictionary
lesson: 15053
title: Looking back in retrospect
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Retrospect is a noun that means looking back on something after it has happened. You will mostly meet it in the phrase «in retrospect». «In retrospect, I should have revised more for the spelling test.» The words in retrospect tell you the speaker is thinking about the test after it is over.
explain: Looking back often shows things differently. Before the test, Sam felt sure he knew all the spellings. «In retrospect, Sam could see that he had skipped the hardest words.» At the time he did not notice this, but after the test he saw it clearly.
explain: Another phrase with the same meaning is «with hindsight». You can use either one in your writing, but do not use them to talk about the future. They always look back.
fact: Retrospect means looking back on something after it has happened.
fact: «In retrospect» means when you think about something afterwards, often seeing it differently.
fact: «With hindsight» is a similar phrase and means much the same as «in retrospect».
fact: Historians often look at events in retrospect and can see causes that people at the time could not see.
fact: Looking back in retrospect helps us learn from our mistakes.
exercise: «In retrospect, the picnic was a bad idea, because it rained all afternoon.» What does «in retrospect» mean here? | When you are just about to start it | When you are planning it for next week | When it is raining right now | *When you look back on it afterwards
exercise: «In retrospect, Ben saw that the map had been upside down all along.» What is Ben doing? | *Looking back and seeing the mistake | Drawing a new map | Looking forward to his trip | Reading a book about maps
exercise: Which phrase means the same as «in retrospect»? | In the middle | *With hindsight | At the start | Ahead of time
test: «In retrospect, the film was much better than I first thought.» What does this sentence show? | The speaker has never seen the film | The film is about to start | *The speaker is looking back and seeing the film differently | The film was too long
test: «With hindsight, Priya wished she had packed a coat.» What does «with hindsight» mean? | *Looking back, after the event | Looking forward, before the event | Looking for a lost coat | Looking up at the sky
exam: Why does looking back in retrospect help us? | *It helps us learn from our mistakes | It helps us forget what happened | It helps us win every game | It helps us make the same mistakes again
